a week and a half before the logo,

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.320
or a couple weeks before
the logo was announced.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.380
Yes, and now we're talking
five or six weeks ago, but.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:41.563
Yeah, I mean, why not, right?

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.660
So there was a tweet that went out

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.823
that essentially said
something along the lines of;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.160
I mean, if you wanna read it

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.610
just so we can get it
exactly right what was said,

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.020
and then we can tell you
what we were trying to say

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:59.293
and then again what we,
unfortunately, miscommunicated.

00:06:59.293 --> 00:07:00.980
I think the big note here for us-

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.930
I don't think we
miscommunicated as much here,

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.450
I think it was just left...

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.543
Too open to interpretation.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.250
I'm on Twitter, but I'm.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.083
Mythical is art.

00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:11.837
I'm searching Twitter on Twitter.

00:07:11.837 --> 00:07:13.920
"Dear beasts, we value your enthusiasm

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.640
and hearing your feedback
on all things Mythical.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.460
However, lately we've seen a
few of you directing questions,

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.450
frustration and even anger
at members of the crew,

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.340
both on their personal social accounts

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.690
and indirectly on public forums,

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.440
which is unfair and not in
the spirit of Mythicality.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.740
Please don't cross those lines

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.710
and always use the
appropriate company channels

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.210
to raise your concerns and
constructive feedback."

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.930
And apparently this wasn't as clear

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:43.530
as we thought it was
when we read it and said,

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.810
yeah, this works because...

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.285
The way that a lot of
people interpreted this

00:07:47.285 --> 00:07:50.240
and it is your right to interpret
it in any way you want to,

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.860
but we're going to clarify
what we were trying to say,

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.130
to try to clear it up.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:55.130
The way that a lot of people interpret it,

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.810
is as if we were saying
that you cannot criticize

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.530
the things that we produce as a company.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:02.700
As a media company who
puts media out in the world

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.590
that we were trying to
police what you say.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:06.930
Of course not.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:09.390
I don't, that's never been our intention.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:10.810
We understand that the whole idea

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:12.980
is when you make
something for an audience,

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:15.310
that audience has an opinion

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.810
and that the audience's opinion matters.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.290
And if it's negative, that matters,

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.320
and we take that into account.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.470
I kinda think that's wrapped up in,

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.140
we value your enthusiasm
and hearing your feedback

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.690
on all things Mythical.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.523
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:29.523 --> 00:08:30.630
Which is kind of exactly what we said,

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.170
'cause I just read it again.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:33.003
Yeah.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.200
The line that we were talking about

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.050
is maybe when it comes to you didn't get,

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:42.000
something customer service related.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.570
Yeah.
Or like,

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.610
I have a question about
my merch showing up

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:50.030
or a stipulation about
something else regarding

00:08:51.916 --> 00:08:54.060
any of the stuff that we do from a

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.363
customer service standpoint.
Yeah, let's be let specific,

00:08:56.363 --> 00:09:00.091
we were talking about the
stuff that we sell, the merch.

00:09:00.091 --> 00:09:01.110
That's what we were talking about.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:03.620
People get upset about
getting the wrong size,

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.183
not getting something on time.

00:09:06.024 --> 00:09:06.857
And being delayed,

00:09:06.857 --> 00:09:09.330
And then reaching out to the
members of the Mythical crew,

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.610
who that is their job, they
work in that department.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.640
But tracking them down
on their personal socials

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.893
or talking about them personally.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.500
Just because you know
that's somebody's job,

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:23.640
that doesn't mean you go to the,

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.460
you cross the line to
their personal socials.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.460
I don't even care if they talk

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.020
about their work and stuff on that.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:32.220
It's like everybody talks about
their lives on their social.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.630
That doesn't mean that you can make it a-

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.343
It's not a valid place
for customer support.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.876
Well, we have provided.
Feedback or complaints.

00:09:40.876 --> 00:09:43.707
We have provided official company avenues

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.260
that you can go through
to lodge those complaints

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.470
and those complaints get
heard and those complaints

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:50.640
get considered and answered.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:51.770
Absolutely.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:55.020
So we wanna, we're sticking
up for the Mythical crew here,

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:58.970
our team, so that they can have
a healthy work-life balance

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:03.970
so that fans aren't coming
into their personal timelines

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:07.940
and in their personal space online and...

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.560
And these are specifically people who

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.920
aren't public personalities.
Making complaints.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:16.920
So, there's a distinction
between someone who has a show,

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.430
what we would call talent,
for lack of a better word.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.650
I hate that word because it makes it seem

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:25.000
like only people on camera have talent.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.080
But that's just the industry term

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.430
for people who have a show.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:33.160
We're not saying you can't
criticize the shows that we make.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.430
We're just saying that if
somebody works for Mythical

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.400
in a non-public capacity,

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:40.990
and then you're reaching out
to them on their socials,

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.570
or you're talking about them publicly,

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.230
we're standing up for them and saying,

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:45.910
they didn't sign up for that.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.300
And we don't want them to be harassed,

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.780
especially because we've
provided avenues and channels

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.840
for you to file your complaints.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.240
It's not just harassment, it's even.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:55.350
Engagement.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:58.520
Even polite engagement
on your personal side

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:02.410
is crossing a line that
we wanna help preserve

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.583
their work-life balance and boundaries.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.510
So when it starts to intrude,

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:10.556
it's like we wanna stand
up for our employees.

00:11:10.556 --> 00:11:12.270
And again, there were some things in that,

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.500
in the way that it's
worded, I completely get it.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:17.300
You could think that what we were saying

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:19.230
is that we don't wanna be criticized.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.780
So if you took it that way, we're again,

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.300
we're blaming ourselves
for miscommunication.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:25.133
The thing that we're learning-

00:11:25.133 --> 00:11:26.600
I'm not being too hard on ourselves,

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.270
but you know, it's always hard

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:30.576
to know how things.
But I am.

